IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap4-s2032`

-- Tests for snap4-s2032.l4. Every expected value is written from the text of lines 2951-2976 BEFORE running.
-- A failing assertion is a finding: no expected value here was edited to match the code.

§ `tests -- s 2032(a)`

-- (a)(1)(A): not later than 1 year after November 28, 1990, which is November 28, 1991.
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(A) the review was completed by the deadline` (Date 28 11 1991)
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(A) the review was completed by the deadline` (Date 1 6 1991)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2032(a)(1)(A) the review was completed by the deadline` (Date 29 11 1991))

-- (a)(1)(C): the regulations require incorporation of systems elsewhere, unless the State documents that an alternative would be less costly.
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(C) the regulations must require the State to incorporate all or part of systems in use elsewhere` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(C) the regulations must require the State to incorporate all or part of systems in use elsewhere` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Secretary's standards define how far modification is paid for; the standards are not in the sources.
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(C) payments will be made under section 2025(a) or 2025(g) for the modification` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(C) payments will be made under section 2025(a) or 2025(g) for the modification` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(C) payments will be made under section 2025(a) or 2025(g) for the modification` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (a)(1)(D): proposed systems meet the standards for timely implementation.
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(D) the system must meet the Secretary's standards for timely implementation of proper changes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(D) the system must meet the Secretary's standards for timely implementation of proper changes` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (a)(1)(E): the approval criteria include cost effectiveness; the State documents actual cost and benefits on implementation.
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(E) the criteria for the approval of a system under section 2025(g) must include the criterion` `s 2032(a)(1)(E) the cost effectiveness of the proposed system` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(E) the criteria for the approval of a system under section 2025(g) must include the criterion` `s 2032(a)(1)(E) any other criterion` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(E) the State must document the actual cost and benefits of the system` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(1)(E) the State must document the actual cost and benefits of the system` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (a)(2): reviews to ensure two named things; a third is not spoken of.
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(2) the Secretary must conduct the review to ensure the purpose` `s 2032(a)(2)(A) systems comply with conditions of initial funding approvals` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(2) the Secretary must conduct the review to ensure the purpose` `s 2032(a)(2)(B) systems adequately support program delivery in compliance with this chapter and regulations issued under this chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(a)(2) the Secretary must conduct the review to ensure the purpose` `s 2032(a)(2) some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `tests -- s 2032(b)`

-- (b)(2): within the reasonable period the Secretary determined (here 180 days).
#ASSERT `s 2032(b)(2) the State implemented the standards within the period the Secretary determined` 180 180
#ASSERT `s 2032(b)(2) the State implemented the standards within the period the Secretary determined` 180 90
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2032(b)(2) the State implemented the standards within the period the Secretary determined` 180 181)
-- (b)(3): periodic reviews to ensure compliance with the standards.
#ASSERT `s 2032(b)(3) the Secretary must conduct the review` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(b)(3) the Secretary must conduct the review` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `tests -- s 2032(c)`

-- (c): not later than October 1, 1993; and on the extent to which State agencies have developed effective systems.
#ASSERT `s 2032(c) the report was made by the deadline` (Date 1 10 1993)
#ASSERT `s 2032(c) the report was made by the deadline` (Date 30 9 1993)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2032(c) the report was made by the deadline` (Date 2 10 1993))
#ASSERT `s 2032(c) the report is the report the text requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2032(c) the report is the report the text requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
